From db909528d4635c9022f432c4fb771c9578618572 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Jun 2025 17:23:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 352/913] drivers: stm32_uart: wait TC bit during console flush

TXFE bit does not take into account the shift register after the FIFO.
But if we wait TC bit, we are sure that the last bit have left the UART.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 7b0ed8c5f69116966fe8a90f74252cb3268cfec0 drivers: stm32_uart: wait TC bit during console flush]
Signed-off-by: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I9c0a463df4be73e23f1124ec099847125343fe58
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/501258
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Patrick DELAUNAY <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
---
 core/drivers/stm32_uart.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/stm32_uart.c b/core/drivers/stm32_uart.c
index 9880d8ef2..8cc6957f8 100644
--- a/core/drivers/stm32_uart.c
+++ b/core/drivers/stm32_uart.c
@@ -96,7 +96,7 @@ static void loc_flush(struct serial_chip *chip)
 	if (!loc_chip_clk_is_enabled(chip))
 		return;
 
-	while (!(io_read32(base + UART_REG_ISR) & USART_ISR_TXFE))
+	while (!(io_read32(base + UART_REG_ISR) & USART_ISR_TC))
 		if (timeout_elapsed(timeout))
 			return;
 }
